WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.584
Effective Articulate 360 course creation starts with instructional purpose, not tool exploration.

2
00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:14.928
Before choosing screens or interactions, define the learner, the performance goal, the scope, and the completion requirement.

3
00:00:14.928 --> 00:00:22.737
A course becomes easier to build and review when everyone agrees on what learners should be able to do after completing it.

4
00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:36.440
Strong courses combine clear objectives, structured content, useful narration, purposeful media, meaningful interactions, aligned assessment, accessibility, stakeholder review, and quality assurance.

5
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.650
None of these pieces need to be complicated, but each one matters.

6
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.248
Weak planning can make a beautiful course ineffective.

7
00:00:44.248 --> 00:00:48.535
Strong planning can make a simple course practical and memorable.

8
00:00:48.535 --> 00:00:50.832
The goal is not to use every feature.

9
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:58.257
The goal is to build a learning experience that learners can understand, complete, apply, and revisit when needed.

10
00:00:58.257 --> 00:01:01.932
Rapid responsive courses may be ideal for some projects.

11
00:01:01.932 --> 00:01:08.516
Custom slide-based courses may be better for simulations, branching, or specialized interactions.

12
00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:11.654
The best choice depends on the learning problem.

13
00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:14.181
A durable course is also maintainable.

14
00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:19.693
Keep narration, media, source files, comments, and publishing settings organized.

15
00:01:19.693 --> 00:01:23.214
Check accessibility and LMS behavior before release.

16
00:01:23.214 --> 00:01:28.420
Use review feedback to improve clarity instead of simply collecting approvals.

17
00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:35.999
When the design stays focused on learner needs, the authoring tool becomes a practical means to an instructional end.

18
00:01:35.999 --> 00:01:40.898
The practical takeaway is simple: design decisions should be explainable.

19
00:01:40.898 --> 00:01:44.190
If a module exists, it should support an objective.

20
00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.329
If media is used, it should clarify or reinforce.

21
00:01:47.329 --> 00:01:52.305
If an interaction is included, it should create useful thinking or practice.

22
00:01:52.305 --> 00:01:58.735
If a quiz question appears, it should measure something the learner was actually expected to learn.
